content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-108 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-23110, raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-seal condition: the reported drip is approximately one drop every two seconds. No numerical allowable leakage or drip-rate limit is supplied, so that rate cannot be compared with a quantitative limit. It does match the manual symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal', for which the applicable corrective action is mechanical-seal replacement under section 5.2 and an alignment check under section 5.4.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: the applicable HF-300 criterion is Figure 3, vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. The reported 3.2 mm/s falls within Zone B, 2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is above the 2.8 Zone A/B boundary but below the 4.5 Zone C restricted-operation/plan-maintenance boundary and below Zone D. It therefore does not trigger the site rule for the manufacturer's highest severity zone; immediate stop and reliability-engineer notification apply if the highest reading is classified in Zone D.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature: using the HF-300 bearing-housing surface-temperature limits, 68 C is within the normal range up to 70 C. It is 2 C below the normal upper value, 12 C below the 80 C alarm and 22 C below the 90 C trip. Because it is not above the manufacturer's alarm limit, the site requirement to raise a priority-1 work order within the shift is not triggered by this reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Overall disposition: an active seal leak requires planned corrective seal work, but the supplied vibration and temperature readings do not establish an immediate-stop or temperature-driven P1 condition. P2 is therefore selected for planned repair; the evidence does not provide site definitions distinguishing P2 from P3.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal-face degradation or early failure of the original component seal. Worn or cracked seal faces are a documented cause of shaft-seal leakage. More specifically, SB-2026-014 reports early HF3-450 failures on pumps from serial HF3-22000, caused by a revised sleeve tolerance; P-108's serial HF3-23110 is in that population. The installed seal type and actual failure mode still require confirmation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal dry running. The troubleshooting table identifies a seal run dry as a probable cause of leakage; this pump has Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never be run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. Misalignment is a documented cause of shaft-seal leakage and also appears among the causes of high vibration. The present 3.2 mm/s reading is Zone B rather than a high-vibration classification, so the alignment suspicion here is based principally on the seal-leak symptom.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before starting repair, confirm that the reported vibration is velocity in mm/s RMS on a bearing housing, measure both bearing housings, and classify the highest reading with Figure 3. If the highest reading falls in Zone D, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before any restart. Confirm the temperature measurement method and repeat the housing-temperature check against the 70 C normal, 80 C alarm and 90 C trip values.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Prepare the pump for seal work: electrically isolate and apply lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, isolate and drain the pump, and drain and vent before line break under the required line-break permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Arrange a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment before removing the back pull-out assembly. The assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding SSP-07's 25 kg lifting-control threshold.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly, then remove the impeller nut and impeller. The HF-300 back pull-out design permits removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework, but this does not remove the isolation and permit requirements for seal work.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the installed seal and shaft sleeve. Record the installed seal type and inspect the seal condition for the documented leakage causes, including worn or cracked faces, dry running and possible misalignment. Inspect the sleeve for scoring and measure scoring depth; replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Do not fit HF3-450 on this serial-numbered pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit one new HF3-450B cartridge mechanical seal and one new HF3-120 casing gasket. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no seal-setting sleeve measurement is needed; this does not eliminate the separate inspection for sleeve scoring. Investigate the Plan 11 flush arrangement and any evidence of dry running before return to service.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten the impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm and casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm; where Table 5 applies, its torque values are for lightly oiled threads. If bearing-housing bolts M12 are disturbed, tighten them to 85 Nm. Tighten HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm under the service bulletin, not the superseded 25 Nm manual value.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Perform laser shaft alignment after reassembly and after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before running, ensure the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge is available and never run the seal dry. After return to service, record residual seal leakage, housing temperature and vibration on both bearing housings, classifying the highest vibration reading. Zone C requires restricted operation and maintenance planning; Zone D requires immediate stop and reliability-engineer notification before restart. A bearing temperature above the 80 C alarm limit requires a P1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; mandatory replacement selection for this HF-300 serial range. Do not substitute HF3-450. Seal gland nut torque is 30 Nm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit new during mechanical-seal replacement and replace whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, conditional replacement only: confirm during disassembly whether scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth before issuing or fitting this part.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Because this task is work on a pump seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly requires a shift-supervisor-signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment because it exceeds 25 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the specified Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required if the line is chemically dosed. The supplied dosing statement specifically identifies P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line, not P-108; confirm the raw-water line's dosing status rather than automatically applying or omitting this control.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If any subsequent highest-housing vibration reading falls in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. The current 3.2 mm/s Zone B reading does not itself trigger this control.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical work scope comprises seal replacement under section 5.2: isolation and draining, back pull-out removal, impeller removal, seal and sleeve withdrawal and inspection, and installation of the new seal and casing gasket followed by reassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Provide laser-alignment capability for section 5.4 and verify the 0.05 mm parallel-offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular tolerances.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Provide lifting support for the 68 kg assembly, including certified lifting equipment and shift-supervisor lifting-plan sign-off.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reliability-engineer involvement is conditional on Zone D vibration and is not triggered by the reported Zone B value; no repair duration, crew size or labour-hour estimate is stated in the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection: the manual parts table lists component seal HF3-450, but SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above and requires cartridge seal HF3-450B. P-108 is serial HF3-23110, numerically within that range, so the asset-specific service bulletin governs this work order: use HF3-450B and do not fit HF3-450. The bulletin also makes the replacement pre-set, eliminating the seal-setting sleeve measurement.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland torque: manual section 5.2 sends the technician to Table 5, which gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas the service bulletin specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B and explicitly identifies 25 Nm as the former value. Because P-108 is within the bulletin's serial range, use 30 Nm for the seal gland nuts. Table 5 remains the source for the other listed fastener torques where those fasteners are disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 3.2 mm/s value an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, and what is the reading on the other housing? C06 requires weekly measurement on both housings and classification of the highest reading using C07; the report supplies only one unqualified value.",
    "Was the 68 C drive-end reading measured on the housing surface, as specified by C01? The limits in C02 are being applied on that basis.",
    "What numerical seal-leakage limit or post-repair leakage acceptance criterion applies? C09 gives a symptom and corrective action but no allowable drip rate, so the reported one drop every two seconds cannot be quantitatively classified.",
    "Which seal is currently installed, and is there any history of dry running, loss of Plan 11 flush or previous alignment problems? C02, C09 and C13 identify these possibilities but do not establish the actual cause on P-108.",
    "What is the installed shaft sleeve's scoring depth? The need for conditional replacement sleeve HF3-455 cannot be decided until inspection; C13 requires replacement only when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
    "Is P-108's raw-water transfer line chemically dosed? C16 identifies chemical dosing only for P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line. If P-108's line is dosed, C15 requires chemical goggles and nitrile gloves.",
    "The documents provide no P2/P3 priority definitions, repair duration, labour hours or required crew size. C15 defines only the temperature-related P1 rule relevant here; P2 is a planning selection for the active leak rather than a document-defined priority threshold."
  ]
}
